From: Peripheral Pretender setup <pp-setup@localhost>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 05:53:20 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] hw/avr: Nano Base AN and socket 2's UART on the AVR64EA48
 Curiosity Nano

AN of the Nano Base's sockets 1-3 is PD4, PD5 and PD7 (ADC0 AIN4, AIN5,
AIN7; user guide Figure 7-5), as an analog input and as a digital pad, so
the POT, DC Motor and Rotary Clicks plug in. Socket 2's UART is USART1 on
PC0/PC1, the debugger's virtual COM port lines: a UART Click there shares
them with serial 0 through a new chardev-mikrobus-share
(mikrobus_uart_share()), which sends what the MCU transmits to both and
passes what either sends to the MCU.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
